Fishing activity


Code
fishing &lt;- all_years |&gt;
  dplyr::filter(fishing_activity) |&gt;
  dplyr::group_by(lon_center, lat_center) |&gt;
  dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop")

map_pixels(fishing, "Fishing kW-hours per pixel")





Kilowatt-hours of fishing activity, January 2015 to August 2026: fishing vessels at positions GFW’s model scores as fishing.





Year by year


Code
fishing_by_year &lt;- fishing_yearly |&gt;
  dplyr::group_by(year, lon_center, lat_center) |&gt;
  dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(
    year_label = dplyr::if_else(year == max(year), paste(year, "(Jan to Aug)"), as.character(year))
  )

map_pixels(fishing_by_year, "Fishing kW-hours per pixel") +
  ggplot2::facet_wrap(ggplot2::vars(year_label), ncol = 4) +
  ggplot2::theme(axis.text = ggplot2::element_blank())





Kilowatt-hours of fishing activity per year. 2026 covers January to August only.

Non-fishing activity


Code
non_fishing &lt;- all_years |&gt;
  dplyr::filter(!fishing_activity) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(group = activity_group(vessel_class, fishing_activity))

non_fishing_panels &lt;- dplyr::bind_rows(
  non_fishing |&gt;
    dplyr::group_by(lon_center, lat_center) |&gt;
    dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
    dplyr::mutate(panel = "All non-fishing activity"),
  non_fishing |&gt;
    dplyr::group_by(panel = as.character(group), lon_center, lat_center) |&gt;
    dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop")
) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(panel = factor(panel, levels = c("All non-fishing activity", group_levels[-1])))

map_pixels(non_fishing_panels, "Non-fishing kW-hours per pixel") +
  ggplot2::facet_wrap(ggplot2::vars(panel), ncol = 2) +
  ggplot2::theme(axis.text = ggplot2::element_blank())





Kilowatt-hours of non-fishing activity, January 2015 to August 2026, all on one colour scale. Other non-fishing includes tugs, patrol and research vessels, and fishing vessels when they aren’t fishing.

By vessel type


Code
top_n_classes &lt;- 10
activity_levels &lt;- c("Fishing activity", "Non-fishing activity")

by_class &lt;- all_years |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(
    activity = factor(
      dplyr::if_else(fishing_activity, activity_levels[1], activity_levels[2]),
      levels = activity_levels
    )
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::group_by(activity, vessel_class) |&gt;
  dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  dplyr::group_by(activity) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(
    vessel_type = dplyr::if_else(
      dplyr::min_rank(dplyr::desc(kw_hours)) &lt;= top_n_classes,
      pretty_class(vessel_class),
      "Other"
    )
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::group_by(activity, vessel_type) |&gt;
  dplyr::summarise(kw_hours = sum(kw_hours), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  # Order bars within each panel, largest at the top and Other at the bottom
  dplyr::mutate(
    sort_value = dplyr::if_else(vessel_type == "Other", -Inf, kw_hours),
    bar = paste(activity, vessel_type, sep = "___")
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::arrange(activity, sort_value) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(bar = factor(bar, levels = unique(bar)))

ggplot2::ggplot(by_class, ggplot2::aes(x = kw_hours, y = bar)) +
  ggplot2::geom_col(fill = data_colour, width = 0.7) +
  ggplot2::facet_wrap(ggplot2::vars(activity), scales = "free", ncol = 2) +
  ggplot2::scale_y_discrete(labels = function(x) sub("^.*___", "", x)) +
  ggplot2::scale_x_continuous(
    labels = short_number,
    breaks = scales::breaks_extended(n = 4),
    expand = ggplot2::expansion(mult = c(0, 0.1))
  ) +
  ggplot2::labs(x = "kW-hours", y = NULL) +
  theme_site() +
  ggplot2::theme(panel.grid.major.y = ggplot2::element_blank())





Kilowatt-hours by vessel type, January 2015 to August 2026. The two panels have different scales. Non-fishing activity includes fishing vessels’ time when they aren’t fishing. Classes outside the top ten in a panel are grouped as Other.
